<card id="c" title="Gusinje Bus Stop: Where the Bus to Podgorica and Plav Actually Stops">
<do type="prev" label="Back"><prev/></do>
<p><b>Is there a bus station in Gusinje?</b> No. Map apps show a point called &quot;Autobuska stanica Gusinje&quot; but there is no building, no ticket office and no staff. It is a piece of road.</p>
<p><b>What time does the bus leave Gusinje?</b> Four a day. 05:46, 12:21 and 15:45 with Elan Company, then 16:45 with Arena Tours. All of them call at Plav first.</p>
<p><b>How long does the bus from Gusinje to Podgorica take?</b> About four hours. The direct distance is only 47 km, but there is no bus route over the mountains, so it loops north through Plav, Berane, Mojkovac and Kolasin, roughly 195 km of road.</p>
<p><b>How much is the ticket from Gusinje to Podgorica?</b> Mine cost 15.80 euros online at busticket4.me. You can also pay the driver in cash when you board. Luggage is 2 euros extra, also to the driver.</p>
